[hermes:err-live] ## Summary
[hermes:err-live] This PR introduces hardware classification for PyTorch test classes.
[hermes:err-live] Tests can now explicitly declare their hardware classification through a `hw_classification` class attribute, and users can filter which categories of tests to run via `--hw-classification`.
[hermes:err-live] When `--hw-classification` is not specified, all existing test discovery and execution paths remain unchanged.
[hermes:err-live] ---
[hermes:err-live] ## Changes
[hermes:err-live] ### Hardware classification
[hermes:err-live] Added `HardwareClassification` with three categories:
[hermes:err-live] - `GENERIC`
[hermes:err-live] - `DEVICE_GENERIC`
[hermes:err-live] - `CPU`, `CUDA`, `XPU`, `MPS` — specific built-in device types
[hermes:err-live] ### Test filtering
[hermes:err-live] Added `--hw-classification` support across unittest, pytest, subprocess, parallel, XML, repeat, and `run_test.py` execution paths. Filtering is implemented through:
[hermes:err-live] - `HardwareClassificationTestLoader`
[hermes:err-live] - `HardwareClassificationPytestPlugin`
[hermes:err-live] - `_filter_suite_by_hw_classification()`
[hermes:err-live] ### Tests
[hermes:err-live] Added unit tests in `test/test_testing.py` covering:
[hermes:err-live] - hardware classification filtering
[hermes:err-live] - inherited hw classification metadata
[hermes:err-live] ### Initial rollout
[hermes:err-live] Annotated test classes in `test/profiler/test_memory_profiler.py` to validate the rollout and provide an initial set of classified tests.
[hermes:err-live] ---
