[hermes:err-live] #### Comments (last 8 of 16)
[hermes:err-live] - **@fffrog:** > For the GENERIC tests, I guess it's the case that we don't care which device is used because it "doesn't matter" for the functionality under test? And for DEVICE_GENERIC tests, we specifically care that the functionality under test works across devices? Imo in the ideal case (infinite resources), the entire set of GENERIC tests would be in DEVICE_GENERIC to maximize coverage, as it doesn't hurt to ensure some piece of functionality works across devices. So it seems to me that the distinction on which tests are GENERIC and which are DEVICE_GENERIC isn't clear-cut and depends on the details to determine the right test resources / coverage tradeoff; thus it seems like there will be consistent contention on which class a test should be in if we migrate tests over to this classification.
